              "step3": "Đoạn 7: Those after fuller cartographic detail may feel a little short-changed , and yet in Joos van Dael the author plainly recognised a kindred spirit . It was van Dael , a craftsman of Bruges, who in 1489 produced the Wereldbol — the oldest globe still in existence — its surface exquisitely finished by a team of painters and other artisans , only for news to arrive that a westbound expedition had blundered upon unknown lands that very year , leaving his creation obsolete on the day it was done . A comparable , if still grander, single-mindedness marks the labours of the Venetian mapmaker Ludovico Farsetti , who in the eighteenth century built a pair of globes for an Austrian archduke . Câu (2)–(3): Brandt xem Joos van Dael là người đồng điệu ; câu sau kể về công trình của van Dael. Câu (4): Ludovico Farsetti cũng được gắn với sự kiên tâm tương tự . Hai người làm quả địa cầu thời trước được nhắc đến để làm nổi bật nét tương đồng với Brandt .",
