              "step1": "Tên đang xử lý: Naledi Mokoena, Farid Haddad and Dr Wei Lin . Bài nhắc đến nhóm tác giả này ở đoạn E; lời dẫn “they add” cũng chỉ cả nhóm.",
              "step2": "In one much-quoted paper, Naledi Mokoena and Farid Haddad of the Ocean Justice Initiative , writing with Dr Wei Lin of the Institute for Marine Governance in Kiel , argue that this ‘new gold rush beneath the waves’ merely repeats the old story of resource grabs : scant regard for the damage done to nature or society , and the pushing aside of indigenous peoples . So little is known of the deep seabed , they add , that the far side of the Moon , the plains of Mars, even the surface of Mercury have been mapped in sharper detail — a gap that leads them to call the deep ocean a place where ‘we still cannot say what it is we are missing.’ Câu (2): nhóm tác giả phê phán việc khai thác dưới biển vì ít quan tâm đến thiệt hại cho thiên nhiên và xã hội. Câu (3): cùng nhóm bổ sung rằng các địa điểm ngoài không gian được lập bản đồ chi tiết hơn đáy biển . 🔎 Khớp với statement 6: Little attention is being paid to the harm that seabed operations may do to nearby places and the people living there . Đối chiếu paraphrasing: Little attention scant regard seabed operations new gold rush beneath the waves nearby places and the people living there nature or society distant worlds in space the far side of the Moon better than in sharper detail the floor of our own seas the deep seabed distant worlds in space the far side of the Moon better than in sharper detail the floor of our own seas the deep seabed 🔎 Khớp với statement 9: Scientists understand distant worlds in space better than they understand the floor of our own seas .",
