              "step4": "‘What we’re really asking,’ says Valente, a marine pharmacologist at the Atlantic Biomedical Institute in Lisbon, ‘is whether more medicines are waiting down there , and whether we can reach them before the place is ruined for good .’ He is among the many scientists calling for deep-sea mining to be halted while its costs and benefits are properly weighed . Handled this way, he suggests, the sea’s living riches might prove worth far more than its ores . Câu (1): Câu (1)–(2), đoạn C: nêu khả năng tìm thêm thuốc, rồi đề xuất tạm dừng khai thác để cân nhắc chi phí và lợi ích. Câu (3): Câu (3), đoạn C: tài nguyên sinh học của biển có thể đáng giá hơn quặng . 🔎 Khớp với statement 7: The sea may hold resources of greater value than its metals . Đối chiếu paraphrasing: resources living riches may might greater value than its metals worth far more than its ores"
