              "step1": "Đoạn C: With the industry already in retreat, four brothers set out to breathe life back into steam . Cornelius Reyburn and his three siblings , still schoolboys, put together their first steam car between 1903 and 1906 in the cellar of the family home in Yorkshire . It was assembled from parts salvaged from a scrapped early steamer, rebuilt to power an engine of the brothers' own design . This first attempt ran poorly , but the Reyburns pressed on , producing a second and then a third prototype over the next few years . That third car , which they called the Mark II, still could not match the convenience of a petrol engine ; even so , the many advances it showed over earlier steam vehicles earned it write-ups in the motoring trade press . In several respects it simply outdid its petrol-driven rivals . Where combustion engines rattled and gave off the smell of burnt fuel , the Reyburns' high-pressure steam turned the pistons almost soundlessly . Most striking was its speed : from a standstill it could reach fifty miles an hour in roughly eighteen seconds, described as 'acceleration of a remarkable order' by The Carriage and Motor Gazette in 1911 . Câu (1)–(4): giới thiệu quá trình phát triển xe hơi nước; chiếc đầu chạy kém nhưng anh em Reyburn tiếp tục đến mẫu thử thứ ba. Câu (5): dù chưa tiện bằng động cơ xăng, các cải tiến giúp mẫu xe được báo chí viết đến . Câu (6)–(8): làm rõ những ưu điểm nổi bật: vượt đối thủ ở một số mặt, vận hành gần như không tiếng động và có tốc độ nổi bật . Đoạn C — almost soundlessly",
