              "step3": "Đoạn F: Certain stretches of time had left behind a wealth of objects , a sign that people had been busy in the mountains then ; from other stretches there was little or nothing . Sørdalen's heights are forbidding , and in the coldest spells glaciers could seal off the upper passes and make travel there all but impossible , so one might expect people to have kept to lower ground during an episode like the sixth-century cold snap of roughly 540 to 600 CE . Instead , judging by how much they had left behind on the ice , hunters went on climbing into the mountains as often as ever . Câu (2): Có giai đoạn để lại nhiều hiện vật, nhưng giai đoạn khác chỉ có rất ít hoặc không có . Câu (4)–(5): Dù có thể nghĩ người ta sẽ ở vùng thấp khi trời rét nhất, hiện vật cho thấy thợ săn vẫn tiếp tục lên núi .",
