              "step3": "Đoạn F: 'The colder it is , the more slowly the phytochromes revert , so they dwell longer in the active form that suppresses growth — and that is why plants creep along in winter . Warmth speeds dark reversion up , so the phytochromes reach their inactive form quickly and release the plant's DNA , letting genes switch on and growth start up once more .' Câu (1)–(2): lạnh khiến trạng thái kìm hãm tăng trưởng kéo dài, còn hơi ấm cho phép tăng trưởng bắt đầu trở lại .",
