              "step4": "The Nadeauvian view maintains that people are equal not just as human beings but in their actual competencies that any one person would carry out the business of government, or of a jury, or of almost any post of responsibility, as ably as the next . Democracy , read this way, treats its citizens as essentially interchangeable , specialised skills alone excepted ; and even those can be acquired through learning . It follows that institutions apt to lift one group above another are neither called for nor wanted . Câu (1): Câu (1)–(2), đoạn I: mọi người bình đẳng về năng lực ; ngay cả kỹ năng chuyên biệt cũng có thể học được . Câu (3): Câu (3), đoạn I: hệ quả là các tổ chức nâng một nhóm lên trên nhóm khác không cần thiết và không được mong muốn . 🔎 Khớp với statement 12: Any ability can, in principle, be acquired by anyone . Đối chiếu paraphrasing: anyone people are equal + competencies Any ability can, in principle, be acquired specialised skills alone excepted + even those can be acquired through learning favoured over another lift one group above another No group should be favoured neither called for nor wanted favoured over another lift one group above another No group should be favoured neither called for nor wanted 🔎 Khớp với statement 8: No group should be favoured over another by any institution ."
