              "step2": "At one extreme, some accounts break play down into distinct types - physical, constructional, linguistic or symbolic, for instance - in the manner of Radnor and Piek (2011) ; at the other, writers such as Calderwood and colleagues (1998) favour broad checklists , grounded in observation and disposition, meant to capture what every kind of play has in common . Câu (2): Câu (2), đoạn 4: chia hoạt động chơi thành các loại >< cách dùng danh sách tiêu chí của Calderwood.",
