              "step3": "Đoạn 5: For his own picture of human conduct Harlow could offer no evidence at all : by the time he was elected president of the Continental Psychological Society in 1911 , he had , in his own words, ' never once observed a single human being ' , his work going no further than experiments on pigeons .",
