              "step1": "Đoạn A: A run of serious governance failures — governance being the way a company is steered at its most senior level — has left firms in Britain, and in other countries too, with good reason to contemplate a drastic rethink of what their directors do . Nobody would pretend that sitting on a board is straightforward these days . When the financial system collapsed in 2008 , the downturn that followed proved deeper and longer-lasting than almost anyone had predicted , and the many autopsies of the episode cast blame in every direction . Regulators , central banks, auditors and governments alike found themselves under suspicion . As for the directors and managers of the banks , their much-publicised shortcomings were raked over at length in one report, inquiry and commentary after another . Câu (1)–(2): đặt bối cảnh thất bại quản trị và sự phức tạp của công việc trong hội đồng quản trị. Câu (3)–(4): khủng hoảng dẫn đến việc quy trách nhiệm về nhiều phía ; câu (4) cụ thể hóa bằng các nhóm tổ chức bị nghi ngờ . Câu (5): tiếp tục mạch xem xét trách nhiệm, chuyển sang giám đốc ngân hàng. Đoạn A — cast blame",
