              "step1": "Đoạn F: Pay for chief executives has turned into a battlefield on which investors, managers and board members wage set-piece struggles — sometimes out of sight , though more and more often under the bright lights of press coverage . To many observers that openness is precisely what transparency and sound governance demand , since shareholders bring their weight to bear on pay so as to force boards into dismissing chief executives who fail to deliver . Once such votes had been made legally binding , their capacity to strike down a company's pay policies grew stronger still . Chairing the remuneration committee can prove a lonely and badly exposed post , as Margery Thorne discovered at Kestrel Bank : she was obliged to step down after weathering a storm of criticism for defending a huge bonus destined for the chief executive — the irony being that , behind the committee's closed doors, she was widely believed to have argued against it . Câu (1): nêu chủ đề — xung đột về thù lao lãnh đạo , ngày càng công khai trên báo chí. Câu (2)–(3): triển khai sức ép của cổ đông; biểu quyết có ràng buộc pháp lý làm quyền bác bỏ chính sách thù lao mạnh hơn. Câu (4): minh họa bằng việc Thorne phải từ chức vì bảo vệ khoản thưởng , dù được cho là đã phản đối khoản thưởng đó. Đoạn F — Pay for chief executives",
