              "step2": "Even so , painstaking work went into making sense of what these Venus expeditions had brought back . Drawing on the whole body of parallax data , Reinhard Faber , who directed the observatory at Breslau, at last settled on a figure for the AU : 152,900,000 km . Close enough for its time , it sits near the modern value of 149,597,870 km , a figure obtained by radar, which has since outstripped transits and every other technique for precision . Câu (1)–(2): phân tích kết quả quan sát Venus => Reinhard Faber tính ra giá trị AU , tức khoảng cách Earth–Sun. Câu (3): giá trị đó gần với giá trị hiện đại => kết quả khá chính xác . 🔎 Khớp với statement 5: By analysing transit data , he produced a fairly accurate value for how far the Sun lies from the Earth . Đối chiếu paraphrasing: By analysing transit data making sense of + parallax data produced settled on a figure fairly accurate Close enough for its time + near the modern value how far the Sun lies from the Earth the AU",
